From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: point installed libraries at $ORIGIN for the
 shared-prefix repackaging

liblapack.so needs libblas.so.3 (and liblapacke.so needs liblapack.so.3) at
runtime - both pairs built by this same CMakeLists.txt and installed into
one directory, cmeel's shared cmeel.prefix/lib/. Reference LAPACK's own
CMakeLists.txt never sets CMAKE_INSTALL_RPATH, so CMake's own install()
step falls back to its documented default: the build-tree RPATH gets
stripped and replaced with nothing (confirmed from the real build log:
"Set non-toolchain portion of runtime path of
.../liblapack.so.3.12.0 to \"\""). A bare dlopen of liblapack.so (e.g. via
ctypes.CDLL, bypassing any package-level LD_LIBRARY_PATH shim) then fails
resolving its own DT_NEEDED libblas.so.3, even though the file is sitting
right next to it:

  OSError: libblas.so.3: cannot open shared object file: No such file or
  directory

Point every installed shared library at its own directory instead, so each
one finds its siblings there regardless of where this prefix ends up
installed.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [needed for cmeel's shared-prefix repackaging, where several of this project's own libraries cross-link each other outside any standard library search path; irrelevant to LAPACK's own build/test]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 1753fa4..7ff9b08 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -14,6 +14,15 @@ set(
 set(CMAKE_STATIC_LIBRARY_PREFIX "lib${LIBRARY_PREFIX}")
 set(CMAKE_SHARED_LIBRARY_PREFIX "lib${LIBRARY_PREFIX}")
 
+# Shared libraries here cross-link each other (liblapack needs libblas,
+# liblapacke needs liblapack, ...) and this repackaging installs them all
+# into one non-standard prefix directory with no RPATH set otherwise, so
+# the install-time strip of the build RPATH (CMake's own default behavior
+# when CMAKE_INSTALL_RPATH is unset) leaves every one of them unable to
+# find its siblings at runtime. Point each installed library at its own
+# directory instead.
+set(CMAKE_INSTALL_RPATH "$ORIGIN")
+
 # Add the CMake directory for custom CMake modules
 set(CMAKE_MODULE_PATH "${LAPACK_SOURCE_DIR}/CMAKE" ${CMAKE_MODULE_PATH})
 
